WEBVTT

00:02.463 --> 00:04.258
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
FRONT SHRINE

00:04.342 --> 00:05.512
[Sakura] Thank you.

00:06.304 --> 00:09.978
This will allow us to proceed
with the Japanese Relief Program.

00:10.647 --> 00:13.443
I hope I can continue
to rely on your support.

00:13.527 --> 00:14.696
[both gasp]

00:16.241 --> 00:19.581
[Walther] In my opinion,
it's not a bad approach.

00:21.000 --> 00:22.754
It's a modest approach,

00:22.837 --> 00:26.762
but by gaining allies this way, you can
overturn Norland through internal policy.

00:27.429 --> 00:29.643
I'm serious about the Relief Program.

00:30.185 --> 00:31.396
[Walther] Of course.

00:31.479 --> 00:34.820
People are not drawn
to that without substance.

00:34.945 --> 00:35.947
Yes.

00:38.828 --> 00:42.084
[Sakuya] Please... Please
will you lend me your strength

00:43.211 --> 00:45.257
until Sakura is rescued?

00:50.267 --> 00:51.729
[Nichol] <i>Ash! Ash!</i>

00:52.187 --> 00:53.231
Ash!

00:53.315 --> 00:55.737
Look! They've gotten so big!

00:56.195 --> 00:57.489
Isn't it amazing?

00:57.866 --> 01:00.913
We're all family,
so we'll see each other again.

01:01.957 --> 01:04.462
[Ash] I hope we can find them
good parents.

01:04.546 --> 01:07.384
At this rate, our trailer
will be teeming with these critters.

01:07.468 --> 01:11.059
Hey there! We're with
the transport service that was requested.

01:11.685 --> 01:13.396
[Ash] You're really something else.

01:15.025 --> 01:16.152
Hey Ash.

01:16.904 --> 01:20.410
Is there someone who means
more to you than anything?

01:21.454 --> 01:23.333
[Ash] <i>You, of course.</i>

01:23.751 --> 01:24.711
<i>Rozé.</i>

01:27.759 --> 01:28.761
[gunshot]

01:35.190 --> 01:37.612
You deceived me
by pretending to be my brother.

01:38.196 --> 01:39.991
I can't forgive you for that.

01:40.660 --> 01:41.954
-[footsteps recede]
-[exclaims]

01:44.626 --> 01:45.795
[Knightmare powers up]

01:49.009 --> 01:50.888
[Scissorman] <i>Sheesh, close call.</i>

01:50.972 --> 01:53.644
<i>I was worried he'd actually end up
killing you there, young lady.</i>

01:53.727 --> 01:58.529
But Young Ash always was a big softy
when it came to his kid brother.

01:59.071 --> 02:02.244
Even when he was falling apart,
he held on for his brother's sake...

02:02.327 --> 02:04.498
Quite touching, really.

02:05.000 --> 02:08.256
Of course, there's no way
you could've known that.

02:10.260 --> 02:13.266
<i>Now then, I've prepared
some new guinea pigs for you.</i>

02:13.349 --> 02:15.813
But we can't conduct
our experiments in this state.

02:18.401 --> 02:21.240
<i>I'm afraid you'll have to
make your way here.</i>

02:22.367 --> 02:29.215
<i>If you refuse to participate,
I'll just dispose of them like trash.</i>

02:29.298 --> 02:32.012
<i>It's entirely up to you
whether you come or not.</i>

02:32.889 --> 02:35.101
[Scissorman laughs]

02:37.064 --> 02:39.068
[♪ opening theme song playing]

04:11.545 --> 04:12.672
[Sakuya] <i>What should I do?</i>

04:13.256 --> 04:14.551
<i>What can I do?</i>

04:17.765 --> 04:20.896
Glad you could join us, Sakuya Sumeragi.

04:21.648 --> 04:23.986
-Empress Sakuya?!
-What are you doing here?

04:24.486 --> 04:27.994
[Scissorman] Sorry they're not
in the best shape.

04:28.494 --> 04:31.543
Have you no shame doing this?

04:31.793 --> 04:34.465
Enough of that, just show me already.

04:34.966 --> 04:36.343
Any command will do.

04:36.427 --> 04:38.599
[Scissorman] Why not make it
something amusing?

04:38.682 --> 04:39.726
Very well.

04:40.018 --> 04:41.312
I will cooperate.

04:42.064 --> 04:44.193
I will even reveal the secret of my Geass.

04:44.276 --> 04:46.405
But first, release these people--

04:46.489 --> 04:47.867
-[Scissorman] Like I said...
-[grunts]

04:47.950 --> 04:49.286
-[woman screams]
-[gasps]

04:49.453 --> 04:51.207
[Scissorman] enough of that.

04:51.708 --> 04:55.549
Though I must say, the secret
of your Geass does sound intriguing.

04:56.050 --> 04:58.806
Or are you just stalling for time?

04:59.223 --> 05:01.352
It's pointless. Give it up already.

05:02.020 --> 05:03.397
He's not coming.

05:04.776 --> 05:09.368
Trust gained through the power
of a Geass is worth nothing.

05:10.036 --> 05:13.167
Empress Sakuya!
Forget about us, just save yourself!

05:13.334 --> 05:14.546
-[collar trills]
-[Sakuya gasps]

05:14.712 --> 05:18.554
[Scissorman] Utterly useless...
the lot of you.

05:18.637 --> 05:21.518
How about I just kill them all,
so we can reset and move locations?

05:21.601 --> 05:23.312
No! Stop, please!

05:29.074 --> 05:30.076
[Sakuya] All right.

05:30.619 --> 05:33.750
I'll do it... I'll show you.

05:36.506 --> 05:38.384
-[woman] Empress Sakuya...
-[child] Empress Sakuya...

05:39.721 --> 05:40.723
[Sakuya] I...

05:43.436 --> 05:44.814
I, Sakuya Sumeragi...

05:47.402 --> 05:48.404
command you!

05:54.876 --> 05:56.630
Ash!

05:57.130 --> 06:00.470
I, Sakuya Sumeragi,
command you, Christoph Scissorman!

06:01.180 --> 06:02.349
You will serve me as my--

06:02.432 --> 06:03.602
Silence!

06:04.646 --> 06:05.689
[gunshot]

06:08.444 --> 06:15.041
Do you really think...
I'd be... your puppet...

06:20.594 --> 06:22.180
[whirring]

06:43.305 --> 06:44.934
-Ash...
-[Ash] I...

06:46.730 --> 06:49.401
I still can't forgive you
for all you've done.

06:50.445 --> 06:51.447
But...

06:51.531 --> 06:52.950
-[inaudible]
-[Ash] <i>I believe</i>

06:53.034 --> 06:57.250
in the words of Jugo Sumeragi,
the man who saved me!

06:58.127 --> 07:01.718
He said his daughter was kind.
I believe those words...

07:02.385 --> 07:03.387
So!

07:04.181 --> 07:07.646
The choices you make,
the actions you take.

07:07.730 --> 07:11.487
I will watch it all with untainted eyes
and see my promise through to the end!

07:16.330 --> 07:17.499
Because...

07:18.752 --> 07:20.338
I swore to him

07:21.131 --> 07:22.968
that I would protect you.

07:30.358 --> 07:32.237
[Sakuya] Thank you...

07:37.497 --> 07:38.959
[Ash] Moving forward...

07:39.502 --> 07:42.758
for us to work together,
we'll need Rozé's presence.

07:42.842 --> 07:46.473
Until everything is settled,
it'd be best for you to remain as Rozé.

07:46.558 --> 07:47.643
Yes.

07:48.352 --> 07:49.856
[Sakuya] You're right...

07:51.483 --> 07:53.445
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
IMPERIAL PALACE

07:53.530 --> 07:57.245
[Arnold] Report! Our raid successfully
resulted in the elimination

07:57.328 --> 07:59.750
<i>of two terrorist organizations
in the region!</i>

08:00.459 --> 08:04.259
<i>We were also able to crush
the Seven Shining Stars' base.</i>

08:04.342 --> 08:07.975
<i>It's only a matter of time
until we eradicate the remaining rats.</i>

08:08.475 --> 08:11.190
I, Arnold, will personally ensure
that Ash Phoenix

08:11.273 --> 08:14.655
and the remaining terrorists
are completely wiped out!

08:14.989 --> 08:16.366
[Norland] Do as you please.

08:16.450 --> 08:17.995
[Arnold] Yes, my lord!

08:18.747 --> 08:20.667
SEVEN SHINING STARS TEMPORARY HIDEOUT

08:21.084 --> 08:24.216
The Eastern Dawn Brigade
and North Wolf Army have been annihilated.

08:24.800 --> 08:27.430
We've also lost most of our forces.

08:28.140 --> 08:30.646
This is all... my fault...

08:31.146 --> 08:32.315
Rozé?

08:32.398 --> 08:35.029
This is the list of weapons
we managed to salvage?

08:35.112 --> 08:39.204
Yes... It was lucky that we stored
spare parts in a separate location.

08:39.789 --> 08:41.751
[Isao] We should recover them
and begin preparations...

08:41.834 --> 08:42.836
[Sakuya] <i>I couldn't...</i>

08:43.337 --> 08:45.174
<i>I couldn't do anything...</i>

08:46.426 --> 08:48.055
<i>On my own...</i>

08:49.224 --> 08:50.226
<i>I'm powerless...!</i>

08:50.309 --> 08:51.311
[Isao] Rozé.

08:52.105 --> 08:53.858
What are your thoughts?

08:54.276 --> 08:56.573
[Rozé] Well... I...

08:58.367 --> 08:59.829
I don't know...

09:00.706 --> 09:05.590
In our current state,
any plan would likely be meaningless...

09:06.926 --> 09:08.972
I don't want to hear that defeatist tone!

09:09.515 --> 09:11.268
[Isao] I don't blame you
for getting caught,

09:11.351 --> 09:13.857
nor for our hideout
being revealed as a result.

09:14.399 --> 09:15.527
But...

09:15.610 --> 09:19.117
don't forget that our comrades
sacrificed themselves to keep us alive!

09:19.785 --> 09:24.587
And yet you, the one responsible
for our plans, say it's meaningless?!

09:24.670 --> 09:26.173
-How can you--
-Monobe.

09:27.968 --> 09:28.970
Sorry.

09:29.638 --> 09:32.811
No... I'm the one who's sorry.

09:33.813 --> 09:35.942
Both of you, get some rest for today.

09:36.611 --> 09:41.662
But come tomorrow, we'll go back to
the drawing board and keep moving forward.

09:42.163 --> 09:45.587
[Kuroto] <i>That's all we can do for now.</i>

09:49.595 --> 09:52.392
-[Ash] Hold on, hold on. Sorry I'm late.
-[animals whining]

09:53.770 --> 09:54.897
Don't jump on me.

09:54.980 --> 09:56.609
-Okay, okay.
-[Sakuya] <i>My Geass...</i>

09:57.318 --> 09:59.197
<i>My true identity...</i>

09:59.280 --> 10:01.536
<i>Norland knows all of it now...</i>

10:01.619 --> 10:05.919
<i>-What can I do in this situation?</i>
-[Ash] It'll be ready soon.

10:06.002 --> 10:08.883
<i>What do I even want to do...?</i>

10:11.138 --> 10:12.306
[Narah] Are you certain?

10:12.683 --> 10:16.148
I'm sending you
to the United Federation of Nations.

10:16.858 --> 10:20.657
I have an idea regarding how to handle it.
Will you entrust it to me?

10:21.158 --> 10:22.160
[Norland] Fine.

10:23.245 --> 10:24.414
BLACK KNIGHTS HACHINOHE BASE

10:24.497 --> 10:26.418
[Gino] <i>I couldn't believe my ears
at first.</i>

10:26.502 --> 10:31.094
<i>I'm honestly shocked that Neo-Britannia
would propose peace talks.</i>

10:32.263 --> 10:36.647
As a fellow Knight of the Round,
I'm acquainted with Norland.

10:37.566 --> 10:40.029
But he always simply followed
Emperor Charles' orders

10:40.112 --> 10:42.408
and mostly stayed out of the public eye.

10:43.076 --> 10:46.333
<i>It's impossible to read
what he's thinking.</i>

10:47.836 --> 10:52.220
<i>In any case, we must be prepared
for every possible scenario.</i>

10:52.638 --> 10:56.729
<i>Regardless of his true intentions,
we cannot afford to show weakness.</i>

10:56.813 --> 10:59.234
[Cornelia] <i>Negotiations will be held
at Hachinohe Base.</i>

10:59.317 --> 11:01.071
<i>I'm counting on you, Sazanami.</i>

11:01.154 --> 11:02.406
Understood.

11:03.116 --> 11:06.206
If a peaceful resolution can be achieved,
that would be ideal.

11:06.289 --> 11:09.295
But at the same time,
it places constraints on us.

11:10.715 --> 11:12.970
They've dealt us a troublesome card.

11:14.264 --> 11:15.725
[Sakura] Peace talks?

11:15.809 --> 11:17.019
[Walther] Yes.

11:17.103 --> 11:20.276
Lady Narah will go to the United
Federation of Nations as an envoy.

11:20.735 --> 11:24.450
Does that mean our efforts
have borne fruit...?

11:25.244 --> 11:26.246
No.

11:27.708 --> 11:30.547
Norland agreeing to peace?
That's ridiculous!

11:30.630 --> 11:31.632
Hear, hear!

11:31.966 --> 11:35.139
The possibility that they're
plotting something behind our backs

11:35.222 --> 11:36.851
is high, to be sure.

11:37.476 --> 11:41.276
However, with their talk of "peace,"
we cannot act recklessly.

11:41.359 --> 11:45.367
If we strike first, we'll be the villains
who disrupted the peace talks.

11:45.910 --> 11:48.290
Damn it! Those treacherous bastards.

11:48.373 --> 11:51.046
[Oda] Hey! What're we gonna do, Rozé?!

11:51.129 --> 11:52.549
[Shota] Keep your voice down.

11:52.633 --> 11:55.597
Regardless, we lack information.

11:55.680 --> 11:57.141
Nothing from your end, Rozé?

11:58.352 --> 12:00.272
No, nothing yet.

12:01.066 --> 12:02.527
[Rozé] I'll keep digging.

12:02.945 --> 12:05.659
See if I can uncover
anything hidden deep down.

12:05.992 --> 12:07.996
[Oda] Sure thing! We're counting on you!

12:08.831 --> 12:10.502
Well then, if you'll excuse me.

12:10.585 --> 12:13.508
-[Oda] We need more crazy weapons!
-[Shota] What we have now is plenty.

12:16.847 --> 12:18.935
What am I doing...

12:19.018 --> 12:21.272
I need to pull myself together...

12:21.356 --> 12:24.571
[man and woman whimpering]

12:27.744 --> 12:30.834
[Kuroto] <i>The Eastern Dawn Brigade
and North Wolf Army have been annihilated.</i>

12:32.128 --> 12:33.840
[Greede] <i>You ought to think this through.</i>

12:33.923 --> 12:37.304
Kill us Einberg and you'll be branded
enemies of Neo-Britannia.

12:37.388 --> 12:38.808
We'll fight and take it all back.

12:38.891 --> 12:39.935
You really think you can?

12:40.018 --> 12:41.396
I want to stop the F.L.E.I.J.A.!

12:41.479 --> 12:42.691
[Rozé] You really think we can't?

12:42.774 --> 12:44.235
-[Sakuya] Please join me.
-Gladly.

12:44.318 --> 12:45.822
-Empress Sakuya?!
-Empress Sakuya...

12:45.905 --> 12:47.534
Why did you come here?

12:47.617 --> 12:51.249
Please... save us!

12:51.416 --> 12:53.128
[Sakuya panting]

12:55.884 --> 12:57.094
[Sakuya] Don't you dare forget!

12:58.681 --> 13:01.019
[as Rozé] This... is my resolve.

13:06.488 --> 13:07.783
Sakura...

13:08.200 --> 13:09.494
The Japanese...

13:10.204 --> 13:11.874
Everything that was taken from us...

13:12.374 --> 13:13.628
I will take it all back!

13:15.422 --> 13:17.009
[as Rozé] This...

13:17.803 --> 13:19.263
is my resolve!

13:23.146 --> 13:25.317
A FEW MONTHS LATER

13:25.484 --> 13:28.448
[Stanley humming]

13:29.952 --> 13:31.956
-[Norland] Status.
-[chuckles]

13:32.791 --> 13:34.711
[Stanley] All deployments complete.

13:35.420 --> 13:37.133
Boy, I can't wait.

13:37.843 --> 13:40.557
We'll finally be saved.

13:45.650 --> 13:46.652
[Ash sighs]

13:47.194 --> 13:49.115
Everything okay, Ash?

13:49.908 --> 13:51.871
I haven't run into her at all lately.

13:52.204 --> 13:53.373
[Ash] Raspberry, I mean...

13:54.626 --> 13:57.047
I stop by the café
every time I pass by, but...

13:57.131 --> 13:59.218
Could she have quit?

13:59.302 --> 14:01.389
I should've asked
for her contact info back then.

14:01.472 --> 14:03.561
Why didn't I?!

14:03.644 --> 14:05.188
[Rozé] Raspberry is...

14:07.276 --> 14:08.654
me...

14:09.322 --> 14:13.079
You know, I had to hide
my identity back then, so...

14:15.375 --> 14:16.629
Sorry...

14:18.758 --> 14:19.885
[Ash] Since when?

14:20.845 --> 14:22.849
Since... the beginning?

14:23.976 --> 14:24.978
Right.

14:25.563 --> 14:27.191
[Rozé] Sorry...

14:31.115 --> 14:33.746
[pilot] Five minutes until we reach
the target location.

14:33.829 --> 14:34.873
[controller 1] <i>Roger that.</i>

14:34.957 --> 14:36.000
[pilot] Area is clear.

14:36.084 --> 14:37.461
All readings normal.

14:37.545 --> 14:39.800
Requesting partial deactivation
of the Situmpe Barrier.

14:39.883 --> 14:41.177
[controller 2] <i>Request acknowledged.</i>

14:41.260 --> 14:43.056
<i>Partially deactivating Situmpe Barrier.</i>

14:43.139 --> 14:44.768
[controller 1] <i>Partial deactivation
confirmed.</i>

14:44.851 --> 14:45.853
<i>Barrier deactivated!</i>

14:48.943 --> 14:50.947
[pilot] <i>Passage complete.
No abnormalities.</i>

14:51.030 --> 14:52.491
<i>Reactivate the Situmpe Barrier.</i>

14:53.201 --> 14:54.955
[controller 2] <i>Reactivating
Situmpe Barrier.</i>

14:58.587 --> 15:00.800
[facilitator] Now,
to proceed with peace talks,

15:00.883 --> 15:03.597
let us begin
our first round of discussions.

15:04.390 --> 15:07.856
First, we would like to hear
from the Neo-Britannia side.

15:09.568 --> 15:10.987
-Well, then--
-[chairman] Excuse me.

15:12.239 --> 15:15.370
Allow us to go first.

15:16.330 --> 15:20.297
Hokkaido was originally part of Japan.

15:20.840 --> 15:23.178
We recognize the occupation
by the organization

15:23.261 --> 15:27.019
calling itself Neo-Britannia
as a military takeover.

15:27.645 --> 15:33.532
However, we also do not wish for
the current stalemate to go on any longer.

15:34.492 --> 15:36.622
We are willing to consider
a peace agreement.

15:36.705 --> 15:42.341
But understand that we will not accept
any conditions favorable to Neo-Britannia.

15:43.134 --> 15:44.679
What are your conditions?

15:45.305 --> 15:47.351
We have two.

15:47.811 --> 15:50.190
First, the demilitarization
of the Hokkaido Block

15:50.273 --> 15:52.027
and the withdrawal of territorial claims.

15:52.111 --> 15:54.658
Second, the dissolution
of the current government.

15:55.200 --> 15:57.539
[Shiro] <i>What's your move, Neo-Britannia?</i>

15:58.707 --> 16:00.043
Distribute them.

16:01.880 --> 16:04.301
That's exactly the matter
I've come to discuss.

16:05.888 --> 16:08.268
[Cornelia] "Concerns regarding
the deterioration of public safety

16:08.351 --> 16:10.230
due to past anti-Britannian sentiment"...

16:10.313 --> 16:13.737
They've even accounted for
"problems arising on the Britannian side."

16:14.238 --> 16:15.282
We've been outmaneuvered.

16:15.658 --> 16:16.660
<i>Indeed...</i>

16:17.119 --> 16:18.747
[Shiro] They anticipated all our claims,

16:18.831 --> 16:21.377
and the materials they prepared
were indisputable.

16:22.254 --> 16:25.177
It appears we've been blindsided.

16:25.720 --> 16:27.264
I'm assuming that's not all.

16:27.640 --> 16:28.642
No.

16:29.143 --> 16:33.443
There were also conditions
subtly favoring Neo-Britannia.

16:33.944 --> 16:36.950
[Shiro] They were hidden,
difficult to identify at first glance.

16:37.785 --> 16:38.996
Your thoughts, Gino?

16:39.956 --> 16:42.127
<i>It is extremely troublesome.</i>

16:42.211 --> 16:45.635
<i>Not only are they thoroughly prepared,
they have a skilled negotiator.</i>

16:47.889 --> 16:50.101
[Cornelia] <i>Perhaps we should play
whatever hand we can...</i>

16:51.437 --> 16:53.692
[humming]

16:56.782 --> 16:58.451
[sighs heavily]

16:58.535 --> 17:02.710
Well then, I'll be leaving now.

17:02.794 --> 17:04.756
May I have a moment?

17:04.839 --> 17:05.883
No.

17:06.425 --> 17:08.973
Regarding the annotation in Article 3,

17:09.056 --> 17:11.728
could you speak with Lady Luxembourg,
currently detained in the--

17:11.812 --> 17:12.814
[Catherine] Not happening.

17:13.314 --> 17:15.736
You're increasing my workload.

17:16.195 --> 17:20.579
Just stick to your policy-making charade
and try not to do anything unnecessary.

17:21.873 --> 17:23.126
Very well.

17:23.752 --> 17:25.506
[Sakura] Asking you
appears to be pointless.

17:26.173 --> 17:27.384
I'll ask her myself.

17:27.467 --> 17:29.723
Excuse me? What did you just say?

17:29.806 --> 17:32.269
Hey! Get back here!

17:35.651 --> 17:38.156
Is this what you mean
when you talk about strength?

17:38.657 --> 17:42.790
A puppet should act like a puppet
and submit to those stronger than her.

17:43.291 --> 17:47.634
Is forcing others into submission
through violence really strength?

17:47.967 --> 17:49.178
That's right.

17:49.261 --> 17:53.353
Sheer strength that subjugates
and takes what it wants from others.

17:54.188 --> 17:55.357
[Sakura] To me, that sounds like

17:56.108 --> 17:57.862
a lonely kind of strength.

17:58.363 --> 18:00.158
It's still strength.

18:00.659 --> 18:03.414
I know what true strength looks like.

18:07.464 --> 18:09.511
But I also know weakness.

18:10.513 --> 18:12.767
[Catherine] Hey... Wha...
What're you doing?

18:15.438 --> 18:18.821
Please don't look down on others
for their weakness.

18:20.658 --> 18:23.204
[Catherine's father] You mustn't look down
on others for their weakness.

18:31.638 --> 18:32.849
[Catherine] People die...

18:34.184 --> 18:35.353
if they're weak...

18:41.157 --> 18:42.827
[Cornelia] <i>In the second round
of negotiations,</i>

18:42.910 --> 18:44.998
the United Federation of Nations

18:45.081 --> 18:49.089
was again outmaneuvered by Neo-Britannia
and failed to present any favorable terms.

18:49.799 --> 18:51.469
It's practically a game of logic.

18:52.053 --> 18:54.433
[Kaguya] Sounds like you have your work
cut out for you.

18:54.517 --> 18:55.519
Yes...

18:56.020 --> 18:58.191
At this rate,
we'll have peace in name only.

18:58.609 --> 19:02.700
Would you consider returning as chairwoman
of the United Federation of Nations,

19:03.201 --> 19:04.203
Kaguya?

19:22.865 --> 19:24.034
[woman screams]

19:38.479 --> 19:40.191
UNITED FEDERATION OF NATIONS HEADQUARTERS

19:40.275 --> 19:41.277
[Gino] What's happened?

19:41.360 --> 19:42.445
[aide] We're not certain.

19:42.530 --> 19:44.742
We've lost communication
with all other countries.

19:45.243 --> 19:46.412
Do we have any visuals?

19:46.788 --> 19:48.165
[aide] The intelligence team

19:48.249 --> 19:50.879
is now analyzing surveillance footage
from each city.

19:52.550 --> 19:53.886
Have you found anything?

19:53.969 --> 19:56.850
We've just finished salvaging the footage.

19:57.267 --> 19:59.187
[staff] The quality is poor,
but I'll display it.

20:09.416 --> 20:11.378
Can you enhance
the image quality any more?

20:14.761 --> 20:15.971
Rewind the footage!

20:16.055 --> 20:17.307
[staff] Understood.

20:19.687 --> 20:22.108
What the hell is that thing...?

20:23.194 --> 20:24.989
BLACK KNIGHTS HACHINOHE BASE

20:25.783 --> 20:28.454
[Narah] <i>The United Federation of Nations
has a new chairwoman...</i>

20:29.832 --> 20:31.126
<i>Kaguya Sumeragi.</i>

20:31.628 --> 20:34.216
<i>She won't be as easy to deal with
as the others have been.</i>

20:34.299 --> 20:36.261
<i>Negotiations resume in three days...</i>

20:36.345 --> 20:38.224
[explosion]

20:40.103 --> 20:41.230
What the?!

20:41.606 --> 20:42.608
Take it down!

20:45.154 --> 20:47.033
-[alarm blaring]
<i>-Multiple unidentified intruders</i>

20:47.117 --> 20:48.578
<i>have breached the building!</i>

20:48.662 --> 20:50.833
Prioritize the safety
of the representatives!

20:51.250 --> 20:52.628
[Shiro] <i>Escort them to the shelters!</i>

20:52.712 --> 20:55.049
<i>Deploy everyone who can fight!</i>

20:57.387 --> 20:59.015
[Narah] <i>What is going on?!</i>

21:00.101 --> 21:01.730
<i>Is this Norland's doing?</i>

21:02.313 --> 21:03.900
PORT OF KOBE

21:03.984 --> 21:07.282
[Yukiya] Let's go to Kyoto next.
I want to visit Kiyomizu Temple.

21:07.365 --> 21:09.579
Haven't you wandered around
enough for one day?

21:09.829 --> 21:13.754
[Yukiya] Come on, we're finally
in the promised land of Japan.

21:14.379 --> 21:15.381
Akito?

21:15.465 --> 21:16.718
[tourist] Hey, what's that?

21:17.469 --> 21:18.471
[Ayano] What's going on?

21:18.555 --> 21:19.974
[people screaming]

21:22.813 --> 21:24.650
ZILKHSTAN AIRPORT

21:24.901 --> 21:26.403
[children exclaim]

21:26.487 --> 21:28.324
-[child 1] So cute!
-[child 2] What's its name?

21:29.451 --> 21:30.913
Hello, kitty!

21:33.877 --> 21:35.004
[Zero] That's...

21:42.603 --> 21:44.189
BRITANNIA REPUBLIC

21:44.272 --> 21:45.776
[people screaming]

21:46.903 --> 21:48.322
-[explosions]
-[gunfire]

21:50.034 --> 21:52.122
CAPE TOWN

21:52.205 --> 21:53.750
[explosions]

21:53.917 --> 21:55.838
[people screaming, clamoring]

22:02.016 --> 22:03.520
[Mei] I'm serious!

22:03.603 --> 22:05.147
A bunch of strange machines appeared!

22:05.231 --> 22:07.318
They're killing everyone!

22:07.402 --> 22:08.780
[Rozé] <i>W-Wait, hold on.</i>

22:09.281 --> 22:12.203
What do you mean?
That doesn't make any sense.

22:12.287 --> 22:13.455
Please, believe me!

22:13.540 --> 22:16.546
These huge bug-looking machines
are swallowing people up...

22:16.629 --> 22:18.550
[Rozé] <i>A new type of Knightmare Frame?</i>

22:18.633 --> 22:20.637
[Mei] I have no idea!

22:20.721 --> 22:21.723
[Vallen] Get down!

22:23.560 --> 22:25.354
Mei? Mei!

22:30.198 --> 22:32.118
[explosion over call]

22:33.495 --> 22:34.497
-[line trills]
-[Rozé] Mei!

22:36.836 --> 22:38.632
What is happening...?

22:40.510 --> 22:42.514
[♪ closing theme song playing]
